From 1d6444b4ad407420a0a82f20031c4b46c9070f50 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: MicroNUX <micronux@example.invalid>
Date: Mon, 10 Aug 2026 23:00:00 -0700
Subject: [PATCH 22/48] video: fbdev: contain ESP32-P4 display faults safely

Illuminate the panel only after a verified framebuffer or VPG source.

Track applied brightness.

Preserve the last valid producer when I2C completion is ambiguous.

Latch DMA, bridge, scanout, and DSI faults in framebuffer mode.

Avoid false stale faults with six 50 ms stationary samples.

Use both the frame count and live GDMA source address as progress.

The host VPG deliberately bypasses the external DPI input.

Record DPI-only status bits 7 and 19 during that bounded phase.

Keep those same status bits fatal for framebuffer scanout.

Allow one dark first-window bit 19 sample while framebuffer DPI refills.

Require four further clean frames before revealing the framebuffer.

Darken before each source switch.

Restore the framebuffer after every post-switch diagnostic failure.

Count four post-restore frames before revealing the status page.

Log GDMA, DSI, and inherited clock state before stopping a failed startup.

Require reboot after destructive faults.

Linux cannot yet reinitialize the panel safely.

Quiesce IRQ, timer, workqueue, and backlight lifetimes on removal.

Signed-off-by: MicroNUX <micronux@example.invalid>
